WEBVTT

00:00:00.351 --> 00:00:11.071
The new phone view shows one project at a time. The top bar names it, and a tap on the name switches to another project, which the phone remembers. The usage pills sit at the right of the bar.

00:00:12.026 --> 00:00:24.426
Below it, a box says how many agents are at work, with the workstation dots of the desktop status bar. It folds away with its chevron. Unfolded, it lists the cards the agents are on, and a tap opens one.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:36.220
An open card fills the screen right below the top bar, which stays, with its conversation and the microphone as before. In the bar, an X takes the place of the usage pills and returns to the list.

00:00:37.174 --> 00:00:47.814
The project's other cards follow in sections: queued first, then planned. A section shows twenty cards and then Load more. Parked and Done stay folded at the end until opened.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:01:02.960
Along the foot floats the new bar: menu, chat, new card, search, and Needs you, whose bell counts what waits across all projects. The plus stands out of the slim bar a little. Menu, chat, search and Needs you come alive in the next steps.

00:01:03.913 --> 00:01:13.713
The plus makes a new card in the project in view. It opens full screen, without the floating bar, and X returns to the list, where the card now stands under Planned.

00:01:14.666 --> 00:01:21.306
So the phone now shows one project, who is working on it, its cards in sections, and a bar within reach of the thumb.
